{"paper": "RRB-NTPC-UG-CBT1-08-Sep-2025-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "tagged_count": 30, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Which of the following numbers is divisible by 14?", "options": [{"text": "67,94,266", "added": false}, {"text": "71,32,960", "added": false}, {"text": "64,36,639", "added": false}, {"text": "70,48,048", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "Train A leaves station M at 8:20 AM and reaches station N at 3:20 PM on the same day. Train B leaves station N at 10:20 AM and reaches station M at 3:20 PM on the same day. Find the time when trains A and B meet.", "options": [{"text": "12:35 PM", "added": false}, {"text": "12:15 PM", "added": false}, {"text": "12:05 PM", "added": false}, {"text": "12:25 PM", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "If the marked price of a calculator is ₹600 and ₹50 discount is offered on the calculator, then find the discount percentage (correct to two decimal places).", "options": [{"text": "9.53%", "added": false}, {"text": "10.33%", "added": false}, {"text": "8.33%", "added": false}, {"text": "7.53%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "Anubhav and Gaurav start a business. Anubhav invests ₹37,000 more than Gaurav for 3 months and Gaurav invests for 4 months. Anubhav's share is ₹1,745 more than that of Gaurav, out of a total profit of ₹8,725. Find the capital contributed by Anubhav.", "options": [{"text": "₹74,002", "added": false}, {"text": "₹74,122", "added": false}, {"text": "₹74,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹73,800", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "A, B and C started a business investing ₹2,410, ₹1,170 and ₹700, respectively. If B's share in the profit earned by them is ₹1,092. what is the difference in the profit (in ₹) earned by A and C?", "options": [{"text": "₹1,597", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,593", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,595", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,596", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "Find the value of [592 ÷ {12 + 2 × (3 − 7)}].", "options": [{"text": "147", "added": false}, {"text": "145", "added": false}, {"text": "148", "added": false}, {"text": "152", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "The marks scored by 10 students are given below. 12, 14, 16, 13, 15, 14, 16, 10, 16, 12 The mode of the data is:", "options": [{"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Elementary Statistics", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "A bus travelling at 28 km/hr completes a journey in 20 hours. What should its speed be to cover the same distance in 14 hours?", "options": [{"text": "39 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "40 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "50 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "34 km/hr", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "In an election between two candidates, 95% of the registered voters cast their vote and 20% of the votes polled were found invalid. The winning candidate got 59% of the valid votes and won the election by a margin of 1881 votes. How many voters were registered?", "options": [{"text": "13751", "added": false}, {"text": "13750", "added": false}, {"text": "13749", "added": false}, {"text": "13747", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "67.4%", "added": false}, {"text": "68.3%", "added": false}, {"text": "69.8%", "added": false}, {"text": "66.6%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Unknown", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "The LCM of the numbers 2.1 and 0.35 is:", "options": [{"text": "0.021", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0.21", "added": false}, {"text": "", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "The H.C.F. and the L.C.M. of two numbers are 25 and 250 respectively. If one of the numbers is 50, find the other one.", "options": [{"text": "175", "added": false}, {"text": "150", "added": false}, {"text": "75", "added": false}, {"text": "125", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "ABCD is a quadrilateral with ∠ A = 3(x + 2)°, ∠ B = 2(2x − 7)°, ∠ C = 69° and ∠ D = ∠ C − 8°. What is the value of ∠ B?", "options": [{"text": "128°", "added": false}, {"text": "183°", "added": false}, {"text": "122°", "added": false}, {"text": "153°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "A shopkeeper marks a product 40% above the cost price. He offers a discount of 20% on the marked price and sells it. What is his gain or loss percentage?", "options": [{"text": "12% gain", "added": false}, {"text": "15% gain", "added": false}, {"text": "8% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "10% loss", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "The average of first 153 odd natural numbers, is:", "options": [{"text": "153", "added": false}, {"text": "154", "added": false}, {"text": "152.5", "added": false}, {"text": "153.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "If 2 times the age of Ram is 30 years more than 4 times the age of Ramya, and 5 times the age of Ramya is 6 year less than the age of Ram, then what is the difference (in years) between the ages of Ram and Ramya?", "options": [{"text": "17", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "Find the total surface area of a cuboidal box whose length is 84 cm, breadth is 45 cm and height is 25 cm.", "options": [{"text": "14,250 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "14,010 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "14,120 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "14,380 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "Pipe A can fill a tank in 12 hours, pipe B can fill the same tank in 21 hours and pipe C can fill the same tank in 16 hours. The time taken by them to fill the same tank if they operate together is::", "options": [{"text": "", "added": false}, {"text": "", "added": false}, {"text": "", "added": false}, {"text": "", "added": false}], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "The cost of 7 pens and 13 pencils is ₹128. If the cost of a pen decreases by ₹7 and the cost of a pencil increases by ₹2, then the cost of 14 pens and 10 pencils is ₹98. What is the original cost of 9 pens and 7 pencils?", "options": [{"text": "₹117", "added": false}, {"text": "₹112", "added": false}, {"text": "₹111", "added": false}, {"text": "₹116", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "By selling 6 tablets for a rupee, a man loses 35%. To gain 30% how many must he sell for a rupee?", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "Find the simple interest (in ₹) on ₹1,200 at an interest rate of 4% per month for 7 months.", "options": [{"text": "₹336", "added": false}, {"text": "₹28", "added": false}, {"text": "₹56", "added": false}, {"text": "₹48", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "The perimeter of a square is 52 m. Its area (in m2) is:", "options": [{"text": "172", "added": false}, {"text": "168", "added": false}, {"text": "169", "added": false}, {"text": "180", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "4 men can complete a piece of work in 18 days, while 9 women can do it in 8 days. In how many days can 3 women and 3 men complete this work?", "options": [{"text": "17 days", "added": false}, {"text": "11 days", "added": false}, {"text": "12 days", "added": false}, {"text": "16 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "Find the value of: 66−5 ÷ 6611 × 66−12", "options": [{"text": "66−27", "added": false}, {"text": "66−34", "added": false}, {"text": "66−28", "added": false}, {"text": "66−25", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "112x + 140", "added": false}, {"text": "−112x − 140", "added": false}, {"text": "112x − 140", "added": false}, {"text": "−112x + 140", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Unknown", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "", "added": false}, {"text": "", "added": false}, {"text": "", "added": false}, {"text": "", "added": false}], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Unknown", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "Find the mean proportional between 25 and 36.", "options": [{"text": "33", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "Find the simple interest (in ₹) on ₹4,000 at 7.5% per annum rate of interest deposited on 10 February 2024 and withdrawn on 11 April 2024.", "options": [{"text": "51", "added": false}, {"text": "48", "added": false}, {"text": "49", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "A number, when decreased by 7%, gives 2790. The number is:", "options": [{"text": "3000", "added": false}, {"text": "1500", "added": false}, {"text": "9000", "added": false}, {"text": "6000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "The number of prime numbers lying between 472 and 486, both included, is:", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}], "detail": null}